===''Pokémon the Series''===
===={{aniseries|SM}}====
An Aether Foundation Employee first appeared in ''[[SM044|A Dream Encounter!]]''. Several other Employees appeared in ''[[SM046|Deceiving Appearances!]]'', including a disguised {{TRT}}, who had been personally hired by {{an|Faba}} to serve as his underlings. However, they resigned in ''[[SM049|Mission: Total Recall!]]'' upon discovering Faba's plans to erase {{an|Lillie}}'s memories, with them declaring that even they wouldn't stoop so low.

Several Aether Foundation Employees appeared in ''[[SM096|Don't Ignore the Small Stufful!]]''. They listened as [[Wicke]] made an announcement about a missing {{an|Stufful}}. Team Rocket were also seen in their Employee disguises, working under Wicke. They had planned to steal the Pokémon living in [[Aether Paradise]]'s conservation area as an offering to {{an|Giovanni}}, but their covers were blown after they were caught with Stufful. Others appeared in flashbacks, seen releasing a group of {{p|Braviary}} and {{p|Wishiwashi}}.

In ''[[SM116|The Secret Princess!]]'', Wicke was revealed to have been an Aether Foundation Employee back when the Aether Foundation was founded.
{{-}}

==In the manga==
[[File:Aether Foundation Adventures.png|thumb|180px|Aether Foundation Employees in [[Pokémon Adventures]]]]
===Pokémon Adventures===
Aether Foundation Employees debuted in ''[[PASM11|Homecoming and the Brilliant Professional Golfer]]'', where two were seen on a commercial advertising their organization.

In ''[[PASM13|Unleashing the Incredible Z-Move]]'', a group of Employees were seen at [[Aether Paradise]] filming another Aether Foundation commercial.

In ''[[PASM15|Shipwreck and "Oh, What Sharp Teeth You Have, Bruxish!"]]'', a male Employee reported to [[Faba]] about {{adv|Moon}}, [[Professor Kukui]], and [[Professor Burnet]], who had been rescued from a shipwreck and taken to Aether Paradise to recuperate. Faba had his {{p|Hypno}} attack the Employee for failing to use his proper title of Branch Chief as a way of ensuring that he would never do it again. Scared, the Employee apologized for his mistake and ran away.

In ''[[PASM16|A Photoshoot and the Abandoned Thrifty Megamart]]'', two Employees appeared in a flashback where they were seen protecting a pair of {{p|Lillipup}} from a group of {{tc|Team Skull Grunt}}s. They were rescued by [[Mallow]].

[[File:Aether Foundation Employee masked Adventures.png|thumb|left|200px|Masked Aether Foundation Employees in Pokémon Adventures]]
In ''[[PASM22|The Truth and Island Kahuna Hapu]]'', Faba and a group of masked Employees set off to [[Vast Poni Canyon]]. After arriving at their destination, Faba sent a small group of Employees to capture [[Hapu]], the newly appointed [[Island kahuna|kahuna]] of [[Poni Island]], while he and the remaining Employees traveled to the [[Poni Altar]]. Before the Altar team could leave, they were attacked by Moon and [[Anabel]]. Worried that his plans would be jeopardized, Faba had the Employees battle Moon's Pokémon, hoping that the clash would be enough of a distraction to allow him to escape.

After Faba left, Anabel switched out Moon's Pokémon for her own and used them to keep the Altar team busy while she, Moon, and [[Plumeria]] followed after the Branch Chief. Elsewhere, the kahuna team encountered [[Hapu]] and {{adv|Sun}}, but before they could capture their target, a {{p|Xurkitree}} that had been defeated by [[Gladion]] was thrown on top of them. Scared, the kahuna team ran away and was told to join the Altar team and meet back with Faba. Once they arrived, Faba had the Employees join him in battling Moon, Anabel, and Plumeria.

In ''[[PASM26|Adventure in the Dark Dimension]]'', it was revealed that six months after the Poni Island incident, Faba had managed to take control of the Aether Foundation, running it like a dictatorship. Despite this, several Employees refused to fully ally themselves with Faba and secretly planned to stop him. When [[Lusamine]] whet missing, a female Employee and Wicke managed to locate her on Poni Island playing with a group of [[Ultra Beast]]s. Their attempts to dock on the island were thwarted by a {{p|Celesteela}}, forcing them to return to the [[Aether House]] on [[Ula'ula Island]] and meet up with [[Gladion]] and [[Lillie]]. Wicke decided the best option was for her and the Employee to return to Aether Paradise and gather information before making their next move.

In ''[[PASM29|Darkness!! The Mysterious Claws of Necrozma!]]'', a group of masked Employees accompanied [[Lusamine]] and [[Phyco]] to the [[Ultra Megalopolis]] so they could capture {{p|Necrozma}}. After Lusamine fused with her {{p|Nihilego}}, she teamed up with the Employees to attack Necrozma.

In ''[[PASM30|Madness!! Mother Lusamine!]]'', the female Employee and Wicke returned to Poni, only to find it empty. They returned to shore, where they found [[Mina]] and an injured [[Guzma]]. Mina traveled to Poni to meet with the other [[Trial Captain]]s, but mistakenly went to the wrong location. The Employee and Wicke had Guzma taken to [[Exeggutor Island]] to recuperate.

Later, several masked Employees under Faba's command attacked the Trial Captains' group on [[Mount Lanakila]]. With the power of their newly-acquired [[Z-Move]]s, the captains managed to defeat several of the beasts. [[Olivia]], [[Acerola]], and [[Kahili]] instead teamed up with one of the [[guardian deities]] to lead some of the beasts to other islands and battle them alone.

